§ `Section 8 -- what else does the Act leave in place, or change?`

-- s 8(1): section 2 does not affect any right or remedy of a third party that exists or is available apart from the Act.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 affect a right or remedy of mine that exists apart from the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A right that exists only under the Act: s 8(1) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Does section 2 affect a right or remedy of mine that exists apart from the Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(2): section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply where the negligence consists of breach of an obligation arising from a term of a contract and the person seeking to enforce it is a third party acting in reliance on section 2.
#ASSERT `Does section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 not apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am not a third party acting in reliance on section 2: the "where" is unmet.
#ASSERT `Does section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 not apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 8(3): references to an action founded on a contract include an action brought in reliance on section 2.
#ASSERT `Is my action one founded on a contract for the purposes of the Limitation Act 1959` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another action: s 8(3) neither includes nor excludes it.
#ASSERT `Is my action one founded on a contract for the purposes of the Limitation Act 1959` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The period is the Limitation Act's, which is not among the sources; 6 is the figure of this case and not of the Act.
#ASSERT `What period in years applies to my action` TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST 6
-- OUTSIDE THE ENCODING.  I do not know the period: the Act does not state it.
#ASSERT `What period in years applies to my action` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not an action the extension names: no period stated.
#ASSERT `What period in years applies to my action` FALSE 6 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(4): a third party is not, by virtue of section 2(5) or 4(4) or (6), treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of another written law` `section 2(5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- OUTSIDE THE ENCODING.  s 8(4) speaks only of those three routes (section 9, for arbitration, is another).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of another written law` `a provision other than section 2(5), 4(4) or 4(6)` EQUALS NOTHING

